SYNTHESIS
  The q0 origin atom is Vitali-like only after the factorial transform.
  Low factorial moments are the analogue of the lambda/c3/c5-visible
  data: they can be held fixed by higher finite-difference moves B_j,
  while Q0 still changes.  The observed split rows all have positive
  nonorigin atom-cone margin, so bounding the whole missed-count law is
  stronger than necessary.  HYP-2719 should choose the support-size
  carrier packets; HYP-2720/HYP-2721 should tax those packets in the
  factorial-origin basis before scalarizing to Q0.
